House Price Prediction & Data Analysis:

Project Overview:

This project is part of the **Data Science with AI Bootcamp (Day 3 Project Task)**.
The goal is to perform **data cleaning, exploratory data analysis (EDA), and visualization** on a real-world house price dataset to understand key factors influencing property prices.

Objectives:

* Load and explore a real dataset
* Perform data cleaning (handle missing values)
* Generate insights using Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
* Visualize relationships between important features
* Understand how different factors affect house prices

Dataset:

* Source: Public dataset from GitHub
* Dataset Link:
  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nunnarilabs/ml/master/house/kc_house_data.csv

Technologies Used:

* Python 
* Pandas
* NumPy
* Matplotlib
* Seaborn
* Google Colab

Data Cleaning:

* Checked for missing values using `isnull()`
* Removed null values using `dropna()`
* Verified dataset consistency

Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA):

* Generated correlation matrix
* Identified relationships between numerical features
* Analyzed how features like:

  * Square footage
  * Bedrooms
  * Bathrooms
    influence house prices

Data Visualization:

* Heatmap for correlation analysis
* Scatter plots:

  * `sqft_living vs price`
  * `bedrooms vs price`
* Observed strong positive relationships between living area and price

Key Insights:

* Houses with larger living areas tend to have higher prices
* Number of bedrooms has moderate influence on price
* Some features show weak or no correlation

